# 🎮 Number Guessing Game (Level Selection Version)

A console-based number guessing game written in Python. The player picks a starting level, guesses the hidden number using hints, and can earn bonus chances by winning a mini-game.

This is a **practice project** built while learning Python. It uses only core Python concepts and the standard library.

---

## Features

- Three difficulty levels: Easy, Medium and Hard
- Choose your starting level (Easy, Medium or Hard)
- Hint system that gets more detailed at higher levels
- Review messages that tell you how close your guess was
- Bonus chances through Rock Paper Scissors and Snake Water Gun
- Super hints in bonus rounds (range hints and prime/composite hints)
- Input validation and error handling
- Replay option after losing
- Star rating and feedback section at the end

---

## Levels

| Level  | Number Range | Challenges | Hint                                    |
|--------|--------------|------------|-----------------------------------------|
| Easy   | 1 to 20      | 3          | Even or odd                             |
| Medium | 1 to 50      | 3          | Even or odd                             |
| Hard   | 1 to 100     | 3          | Even or odd + range                     |

Each challenge uses a fresh random number. Winning any one of the 3 challenges wins the level.

---

## How the Game Flows

**Starting at Easy**
1. Win Easy and you move on to Medium.
2. Lose Easy and you can choose to replay.

**Starting at Medium**
1. Win Medium and you move on to Hard.
2. Lose Medium and you get a bonus chance.

**Bonus chance for Medium:** win Rock Paper Scissors to unlock a Bonus Medium round with a range hint. Win it to continue to Hard.

**Hard level:** win to get the Gold Medal. If you lose, play Snake Water Gun for a bonus chance, then win a Bonus Hard round with a super hint (prime or composite, even or odd, plus range) to get the Gold Medal.

**Starting at Hard:** this is a single-level run. The game ends after the Hard level, whether you win or lose.

At the end of the game you rate the game from 1 to 5 stars and leave short feedback (5 to 100 characters).

